  SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0

  Resource overlay on Android's package installer: one style, no code.
  Android's install confirmation ("Install this app?") is a DIALOG activity in
  a task of its own, and the container's hwcomposer only gives a wayland
  window to a task that is opaque — a translucent one never reaches the
  screen, so the store that asked for the install waits for an answer the user
  can never give.  Making the activity opaque is what puts it on the screen;
  the shell then gives that task a window of its own, like any other task
  Android opens for itself (AppWindowAbility, "taken over by").

  Listed in ../config.xml: an overlay of a package other than "android" is
  ignored when it only says isStatic (that path is framework-only), and is
  enabled by the partition's overlay config instead.
-->
<manifest xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    package="org.oniroproject.waydroid.overlay.installer"
    android:versionCode="1" android:versionName="1.0">
    <application android:hasCode="false" />
    <overlay android:targetPackage="com.android.packageinstaller" android:priority="100" />
</manifest>
